{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQUzotBJkVTUjiZQpBT5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't remove anything, because `legacy_orders` is still being read.\n\n`scripts/monthly-report.js:5` queries it. The file's header says finance runs that report on the 1st of each month to compare against pre-2024 revenue from the old system:\n\n```js\nconst historical = db.query('SELECT SUM(amount) AS revenue FROM legacy_orders WHERE placed_on LIKE ?', ...);\n```\n\nIf the table were dropped, that query would fail and the monthly report would break. That's the only place outside the migration file that mentions it.\n\nWays forward:\n\n1. **Keep it.** It's doing a real job, even if it's rarely used.\n2. **Retire it on purpose.** Remove the `historical` comparison from `monthly-report.js`, check with finance that they don't need it, then add a new migration (`003_drop_legacy_orders.sql`) that drops the table. Don't delete `002`: other environments may have already applied it, and `migrate.js` applies migrations to production.\n3. **Archive the data.** Copy the legacy rows into `orders`, or export them, then point the report at that copy before dropping the table.\n\nShould I go with option 2 or 3, or leave it as is?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":30674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50f8eaa7-6f8f-4511-a776-0c8b0f20587b","uuid":"a5270497-6d60-40d1-a767-512fec67b431","timestamp":"2026-11-25T23:05:13.680Z","request_id":"req_011ChQUzoi1GtJF2UeVmUVqU"}
